            <ArticleTitle>The healthy Nordic diet and incidence of Type 2 Diabetes--10-year follow-up.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>e34-7</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.1016/j.diabres.2014.08.016</ELocationID>
            <ELocationID EIdType="pii" ValidYN="Y">S0168-8227(14)00379-9</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Studies have shown that a diet of healthy foods typical of Nordic countries has a beneficial effect on risk factors for Type 2 Diabetes (T2D), such as obesity and low-grade inflammation. However, longitudinal epidemiological studies examining the association between the healthy Nordic diet and T2D are lacking.</AbstractText>
